{"id": "EUVD-2026-87321", "enisaUuid": "542294a7-3b3b-370c-bc99-56d099147432", "description": "When the HTTP stream wrapper follows a redirect and the response carries a Location header with an empty value, the redirect code reads one byte past the end of the heap buffer holding the location. The value of that out-of-bounds byte decides which redirect target is built, so a malicious server controls whether the client is sent to the host root or to the current directory.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T20:02:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T20:38:14", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-7875-c8px-7q5f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93682"], "assigner": "php", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "12153d16-2c35-3a2b-bc86-57e53aeeb74f", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.2.* <8.2.34"}, {"id": "67a18ea2-2311-3286-bbdb-652bd65c4e3d", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.4.* <8.4.26"}, {"id": "dd989765-581b-3b9b-97b2-1fc97f9b1c75", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.5.* <8.5.11"}, {"id": "fd025ba8-d94d-35ff-bfa1-b3f4a100a262", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.3.* <8.3.35"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f3ba860f-d940-3a6e-8b5a-4f2fd0e96892", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}], "isExploited": false}